# CAGED: The Major Scale in Five Positions (repertoire plan: st-caged-scale). An original study,
# eighth notes. C major climbs the neck through its five CAGED positions, in the guitar engine's
# order and fingering:
#   C shape  open position, frets 0-3      A shape  2nd position, frets 2-6
#   G shape  5th position, frets 4-8       E shape  7th position, frets 7-10
#   D shape  10th position, frets 9-13
# Each position is six bars: two bars of the scale from its lowest C up to the next C and back
# (the C chord of that shape is the teacher's chord), then a 4-bar original tune in the same
# position. The five tunes join into one melody that climbs from G3 to F5 with the hand.
# Five positions of six bars: 30 bars, as the plan asks.
title: CAGED: The Major Scale in Five Positions
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the CAGED positions of C major
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 7
tags: caged, major scale, positions, whole neck
tempo: 100
time: 4/4
key: C

